<% content_for :title, "Terms of Service · Donna Moneypenny" %>

<main class="legal">
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: October 11, 2026</p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    Donna Moneypenny is a private, non-commercial personal finance tool, run by its owner for
    their own use only. It is not offered to the public, there is no way to sign up, and it is
    free.
  </p>

  <h2>Bank data</h2>
  <p>
    The app reads data from the owner's own bank accounts through Enable Banking Oy, only after
    the owner has given explicit consent at their bank. Access is read-only: the app cannot make
    payments or change anything at the bank. Consent can be withdrawn at any time through the
    bank or Enable Banking, and it also expires automatically.
  </p>
  <p>
    How the data is handled is described in the <%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %>.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The app is provided as is, for personal bookkeeping. Figures shown in it may be incomplete
    or delayed, and the bank's own records are always authoritative.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated at any time. The date above shows the latest version.
  </p>

  <p class="legal-footer"><%= link_to "Privacy Policy", privacy_path %></p>
</main>
